    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `contactPreference` on the owner response \u2014 `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nChanges, each placed where the codebase already keeps that kind of logic:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string field to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it (matching the other derived fields like `displayName`, `locality`, `membershipLevel`).\n\n2. **`util/ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility derivation class mirroring the existing `MembershipLevel`/`CityRegion` utilities: `ContactPreference.of(owner)` returns `EMAIL`/`PHONE` based on whether the owner has a non-blank email.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired the field via a `@Mapping(... expression)` delegating to a `contactPreference(owner)` default method that calls the util, exactly like `locality(...)` and `membershipLevel(...)`.\n\nNo responder or endpoint changes were needed \u2014 `GET /api/owners/{id}` already maps through `OwnerMapper`. Both new tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass.",
